# Code Review: Runtime Metrics Exposure

## Root Cause
The runtime maintains authoritative metrics in `MetricsTracker` (`apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/metrics.ts`) but **never exposes them to the client**. The client (`apps/game-client/src/App.tsx`) currently displays static or derived values (e.g., `runtimeQueueAhead` from config) rather than live runtime state. The protocol (`packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`) lacks a dedicated metrics payload in `session.state` or a new `runtime.metrics` message type.

## Smallest Safe Fix
Extend the existing `session.state` server message to include the current metrics snapshot. This avoids adding a new message type, keeps the runtime authoritative, and requires minimal client changes.

### 1. Protocol Change
**File:** `packages/protocol/src/messages.ts`

Add a `metrics` field to the `session.state` payload type.

```typescript
// packages/protocol/src/messages.ts

// ... existing imports ...

export type RuntimeMetrics = {
  turnsTotal: number;
  invalidOutputCount: number;
  actionAppliedCount: number;
  actionRejectedCount: number;
  queuedActions: number;
};

// ... existing types ...

export type ServerMessage =
  | {
      version: Version;
      type: "session.state";
      payload: {
        phase: SessionPhase;
        paused: boolean;
        preparedSeed: number | null;
        threadIds: { gameplayByAgentId: Record<string, string>; builder?: string };
        connected: boolean;
        runtime: {
          model: string | null;
          effort: TurnEffort;
          tickMs: number;
          schedulerMs: number;
          maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn: number;
          availableModels: RuntimeModelOption[];
        };
        metrics: RuntimeMetrics; // <-- ADD THIS
      };
    }
  // ... rest of union ...
```

### 2. Runtime Change
**File:** `apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts`

Update `sendSessionState` to include the metrics snapshot.

```typescript
// apps/game-runtime/src/runtime/GameRuntimeServer.ts

// ... existing imports ...

private sendSessionState(): void {
  this.emitMessage({
    version: PROTOCOL_VERSION,
    type: "session.state",
    payload: {
      phase: this.phase,
      paused: this.paused,
      preparedSeed: this.preparedSeed,
      threadIds: this.threadIds,
      connected: this.connected,
      runtime: {
        model: this.turnModel,
        effort: this.turnEffort,
        tickMs: runtimeConfig.tickMs,
        schedulerMs: runtimeConfig.schedulerMs,
        maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn: runtimeConfig.maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn,
        availableModels: this.availableModels
      },
      metrics: this.metrics.snapshot() // <-- ADD THIS
    }
  });
}
```

### 3. Client Change
**File:** `apps/game-client/src/App.tsx`

Update the `session.state` handler to consume and display the new metrics.

```typescript
// apps/game-client/src/App.tsx

// ... existing imports ...

// Add state for metrics
const [metrics, setMetrics] = useState<{
  turnsTotal: number;
  invalidOutputCount: number;
  actionAppliedCount: number;
  actionRejectedCount: number;
  queuedActions: number;
} | null>(null);

// ... inside ws.onmessage switch ...

case "session.state":
  setPhase(message.payload.phase);
  setPaused(message.payload.paused);
  setPreparedSeed(message.payload.preparedSeed);
  setThreadIds(message.payload.threadIds);
  setRuntimeModel(message.payload.runtime.model);
  setRuntimeEffort(message.payload.runtime.effort);
  setRuntimeSchedulerMs(message.payload.runtime.schedulerMs);
  setRuntimeQueueAhead(message.payload.runtime.maxQueuedActionsBeforeTurn);
  setAvailableModels(message.payload.runtime.availableModels);
  setMetrics(message.payload.metrics); // <-- ADD THIS
  if (message.payload.phase === "idle") {
    setTick(0);
    setRuntimeAgents([]);
    setCatalog({ prefabs: [], recipes: [] });
    sceneRef.current?.clearSnapshot();
  }
  return;
```

Update the topbar to display the metrics (optional but recommended for visibility):

```typescript
// apps/game-client/src/App.tsx

// ... inside return (...) ...

<div className="game-topbar">
  <span className="pill">Runtime: {connected ? "connected" : "offline"}</span>
  <span className="pill">Phase: {phase}</span>
  <span className="pill">Latency: {latencyMs}ms</span>
  <span className="pill">Model: {runtimeModel ?? "default"}</span>
  <span className="pill">
    Effort: {runtimeEffort} | Scheduler: {runtimeSchedulerMs || "-"}ms
  </span>
  {metrics ? (
    <span className="pill">
      Turns: {metrics.turnsTotal} | Queued: {metrics.queuedActions} | Invalid: {metrics.invalidOutputCount}
    </span>
  ) : null}
</div>
```

## Regression Checks
1.  **Protocol Validation:** Ensure `parseClientMessage` and `encodeServerMessage` still work with the updated `ServerMessage` union (no breaking changes to existing types).
2.  **Runtime Persistence:** Verify `persistSession` still saves metrics correctly (it already uses `this.metrics.snapshot()`).
3.  **Client Resilience:** Ensure the client handles `session.state` messages gracefully if `metrics` is missing (e.g., during a brief transition or if an older runtime is running). The client state update `setMetrics(message.payload.metrics)` is safe as long as the type definition is updated.
4.  **UI Rendering:** Confirm the new metrics pill in the topbar renders correctly and updates in real-time as the game runs.
